DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     NNccrroonn reads the file /uussrr/lliibb/ccrroonnttaabb and, once each minute,
     runs every entry in it whose time fields match the current
     minute, hour, day of the month, month, and day of the week.

     At start-up NNccrroonn sets its user and group id to those of
     user ddaaeemmoonn if that user exists, changes its working direc-
     tory to /bbiinn, and arranges to wake up once every minute.  On
     each wakeup it rereads /uussrr/lliibb/ccrroonnttaabb from the beginning,
     testing every entry; once every command it has started has
     finished, it sleeps until the next minute.

     Each line of /uussrr/lliibb/ccrroonnttaabb has the form

                  _m_i_n_u_t_e _h_o_u_r _m_o_n_t_h-_d_a_y _m_o_n_t_h _w_e_e_k-_d_a_y _c_o_m_m_a_n_d

     The five time fields are separated by white space.  Each may
     be a single number, a range of two numbers separated by a
     hyphen, a comma-separated list of numbers and/or ranges, or
     an asterisk meaning every value of that field.  An entry
     runs only when the current time matches every one of its
     five fields.  The _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is the rest of the line and is
     passed to ppooppeenn so that it runs under the shell.  A percent
     sign within _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is turned into a newline, and everything
     following it is instead fed to the command's standard input;
     a backslash escapes a literal percent sign or continues the
     line onto the next.

     NNccrroonn appends a line to /uussrr/lliibb/ccrroonnlloogg each time it starts
     a command, and, on the hour, a time stamp as well.

